SukiCode - A Modern Systems Programming Language

This project uses multiple licenses for different components:

- Compiler, Runtime, Standard Library: Apache 2.0 + Runtime Library Exception
  See LICENSE_Apache-2.0.txt and RUNTIME_EXCEPTION.txt

- Tools (sukipm, suki-lsp, suki-fmt, suki-doc): MIT
  See LICENSE_MIT.txt

- Language Specification: CC BY 4.0
  See LICENSE_CC-BY-4.0.txt

- Examples and Test Files: MIT
  See LICENSE_MIT.txt

Programs written in SukiCode can use any license, including proprietary
and closed-source licenses. The Runtime Library Exception ensures that
linking against the SukiCode runtime does not impose open-source
requirements on your compiled programs.

See README_LICENSE.md for the full FAQ and details.
